  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate resilient memory institutions protecting &amp;promoting documentary heritage</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNESCO&#x2019;s Memory of the World Programme in the Caribbean will strengthen the capacity of SIDS memory institutions to preserve, safeguard and promote documentary heritage as a foundation for identity, education, research, governance, resilience and sustainable development. Building on work undertaken from 2022&#x2013;2026, the 2026&#x2013;2027 programme will support institutional capacity-building, risk assessments, practical preservation measures, environmental monitoring, digitization readiness, metadata and backup systems, and public access initiatives. The work will help protect vulnerable archives, libraries and collections from climate, disaster and deterioration risks, while developing reusable tools and partnerships to mobilize larger support across the region.</narrative>
  </description>
